1
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:07,500
AgriPricePH monitors and forecasts the retail price
of eight rice types in Metro Manila,

2
00:00:07,500 --> 00:00:13,000
up to three days ahead, using the Department
of Agriculture's daily price bulletins.

3
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:20,000
Every day, it collects its data automatically
from seven official sources:

4
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:25,500
DA rice prices, DOE fuel prices, the exchange rate,
PSA rice stocks, farmgate prices and core inflation,

5
00:00:25,500 --> 00:00:30,000
and the World Bank's world rice price.

6
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:36,500
This page replays twenty days, October 7 to 26,
that the model never saw while it was being fitted.

7
00:00:36,500 --> 00:00:41,000
Each purple point is the forecast for that day,
made the day before.

8
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:46,500
Then the green line shows the real DA price.
The price rises and falls, and the forecast follows it.

9
00:00:46,500 --> 00:00:52,000
On average it was off by about 21 centavos per kilo,
and within one peso on 99% of days,

10
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:56,000
closer than simply repeating the day before's price.

11
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:01,500
The orange line is the same forecast without the factors.
It lands almost on top of the purple one:

12
00:01:01,500 --> 00:01:07,000
for a next-day forecast, the price's own recent movement
does most of the work,

13
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:12,000
and the factors barely change it.

14
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:25,500
Every forecast also comes with a likely price range,
and the forecast page shows which of the three models,

15
00:01:25,500 --> 00:01:33,000
the LSTM, ARIMA or the Kalman filter,
carries the most weight today.

16
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:39,000
AgriPricePH: official data, collected automatically,

17
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:43,000
and forecasts you can check against the real price,
day by day. Thank you.
